   "description": [
    "1 drawing. | Cartoon shows two cowboys (labeled \"Senate\" and \"House\") holding rifles (labeled \"Politics\") reading a notice, \"Check Your Guns Here Before Entering,\" outside a door labeled \"Extra Session.\"  Probably refers to the special Congressional Session called by President Roosevelt after World War II began in September 1939.  As Roosevelt hoped, Congress repealed the neutrality legislation that had imposed an arms embargo. The cartoonist suggests that politics should not be allowed to play a part in this decision."
   ],
