   "date": "1947-01-01",
   "dates": [
    "1947"
   ],
   "description": [
    "1 drawing. | Cartoon shows a hen (labeled \"Rep. Congress\") in her nest, sitting on a door knob labeled \"Campaign Promises.\"  Farmers sometimes put door knobs in nests to fool the hens into thinking they had laid an egg to promote further laying.  In 1946, the Republicans won both houses of Congress for the first time in 18 years.  The cartoonist questions whether they will be able to accomplish all that they have promised."
   ],
